      "problem": "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $1$ pivot column (or alternatively, $1$ non-zero row). \n\nTherefore,\n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\})=1.$",
